# Architecture

## Monorepo Structure

- `apps/` = thin shells (routing, DI bootstrap, app-specific pages only)
- `packages/` = all business logic, features, infrastructure, and shared UI
- Managed by Melos — run `melos bootstrap` after any `pubspec.yaml` change

## Clean Architecture (Feature Packages)

Every feature package follows this layer order:

```
data/ → domain/ → presentation/ → di/ → routes/
```

| Layer | Owns | Must NOT import |
|-------|------|-----------------|
| `domain/` | Entities, repository contracts, use cases | `data/`, `presentation/`, Flutter |
| `data/` | DTOs, data sources, repository impls | `presentation/` |
| `presentation/` | BLoC, pages, widgets | Direct Dio or repository impls |
| `di/` | GetIt registrations | — |
| `routes/` | Route path constants | — |

## Dependency Rules

- Apps import packages — **never** the reverse
- Dependency direction: `apps → feature packages → infra → core`
- No circular dependencies between packages
- Abstract repository contracts live in `domain/` — implementations in `data/`
- New feature = new package (or extend existing feature package) — never put business logic in an app

## App Features vs Feature Packages

- `apps/*/lib/src/features/` = UI pages only (no BLoC, no repository, no use case)
- Real feature logic lives in `packages/auth`, `packages/otp`, etc.
- Reference implementation: `packages/auth/lib/src/`

## SOLID

- **Dependency Inversion**: BLoC depends on `UseCase`, UseCase depends on abstract `Repository`
- **Single Responsibility**: one BLoC per feature flow, one UseCase per action
- **Open/Closed**: extend via new packages, not by modifying core contracts

## Adding a New Feature

1. Create package under `packages/<name>/` with clean arch folders
2. Register in workspace (`pubspec.yaml` + `melos.yaml`)
3. Add DI module `<Name>DI.init()` called from `app_di.dart`
4. Register routes in app router
5. App `features/` folder gets only the page widget if app-specific
